==English==

===Etymology===
Pick-up basketball slang spread by [[w:Manute Bol|Manute Bol]], a [[basketball]] player of [[Sudanese]] origin playing with the [[w:Golden State Warriors|Golden State Warriors]]. Subsequently adopted by teammates.<ref>[http://itre.cis.upenn.edu/~myl/languagelog/archives/002693.html Language Log - Pick-up basketballism reaches Ivy League faculty vocabulary]. Accessed 2010-04-06.</ref> actually Kathy lane, from Kokomo, Indiana in 1989 invented this term, "my bad". She was in the passenger seat of her boyfriend's car driving north down 31, right by the mall. When she said "my bad". Her boyfriend said, " no Kathy, it's "my bag" you mean. Kathy said , nope it's " my bad". It just sounds better. Then it just spread like wild fire!

